<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $173.9 mln Oct 16.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $173.9 mln Oct 16.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $173.9 million surplus on October 16 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON OCTOBER 16</p>
<p>Exports: $162.1 million</p>
<p>Imports: $185.4 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $374.2 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $177 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $173.9 million</p>
<p>OCTOBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.008 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.998 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.451 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.921 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.540 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
